From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:22:50 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: pd-mapper: Add SM6450 support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The service registry files that ship with the SM6450 DSP firmware list
the same protection domains as SM8550's table: the ADSP's root, audio,
charger and sensor domains, with avs/audio on the audio domain, the
CDSP's root domain, and the modem's root domain with gps/gps_service,
at instance IDs 74, 76 and 180. Reuse the SM8550 table.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_pd_mapper.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_pd_mapper.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_pd_mapper.c
index 6384f2719..327ac7421 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_pd_mapper.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_pd_mapper.c
@@ -575,6 +575,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_pdm_domains[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm4250", .data = sm6115_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6115", .data = sm6115_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6350", .data = sm6350_domains, },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6450", .data = sm8550_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm7150", .data = sm7150_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm7225", .data = sm6350_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm7325", .data = sc7280_domains, },
